            <ArticleTitle>A unique rectilinearly π-extended rhodamine dye with large Stokes shift and near-infrared fluorescence for bioimaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10727-10730</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06220f</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The synthesis of a novel rectilinearly π-extended rhodamine dye (TJ730) has been described. It exhibits NIR fluorescence emission with a Stokes shift of &gt;110 nm. TJ730 and its ester derivative are cell permeable, have low cytotoxicity, are biocompatible, and can be directly used as NIR tracers for lysosome staining. Using TJ730 as a precursor, two probes have been prepared for Cu2+.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
